      },
      "summary": "The file has never been analyzed (it has no sqlite_stat1), so SQLite falls back on fixed guesses about how big each table is and how well each index narrows a search. With 3 secondary indexes to choose from, a guess can pick the wrong one, or a full scan. Culprit can't tell each table's size either.",
      "title": "SQLite has no statistics to choose between this file's indexes",
      "verify": [
        "Scan again: the file has statistics, and each table's row count appears."
      ]
    },
    {
      "category": "maintenance",
      "caveats": [],
      "check": "config",
      "confidence": "high",
      "fix": {
        "cost": "VACUUM holds the write lock for its whole run and needs free disk space about the size of the file.",
        "sql": "PRAGMA auto_vacuum = INCREMENTAL;\nVACUUM;",
        "summary": "VACUUM rewrites the file without its free pages. To give space back after large deletes from then on, switch auto_vacuum to INCREMENTAL first (it takes effect with that VACUUM) and run PRAGMA incremental_vacuum when convenient."
      },
